# Phone layout

Phone is the primary surface. A tap or a new form must show its result in the current view. Do not leave it below the rest of the screen.

## Dossier

Wide screens keep the dossier as a right column. Below 900px, a dossier that opens from a tap uses `dossier-sheet` and `useDossierSheet` (`src/components/mobile.ts`). Inicio and Tiempo stay inline: their dossier is always on screen.

## Rosters

Three short columns can stay a table. More columns, or a cell with Editar / Quitar, use `roster-fit` and `roster roster-stack`:

- The identity cell is `roster-title` (no `data-label`).
- Every other value cell has `data-label` with the column name.
- Verbs sit in `row-actions` inside `panel-verbs`, on one line.

```tsx
<div className="roster-fit">
  <table className="roster roster-stack">
    <tr>
      <td className="roster-title">{name}</td>
      <td className="num mono" data-label="Monto">{money(amount)}</td>
      <td className="row-actions">
        <span className="panel-verbs">
          <button type="button" className="panel-verb">Editar</button>
          <button type="button" className="panel-verb">Quitar</button>
        </span>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>
```

## Forms and row actions

A form that opens from a row uses `useScrollIntoView` so it enters the stage. Actions for a selected movimiento use `verb-row verb-row-pin` so they sit above the command bar.

Do not add a second sheet style, horizontal scrolling as the way to fit a table, or new card chrome.
